chem: pinned build backends. Apply from the repository root with
deploy/patches/apply-pyproject-patches.sh (git apply, then `uv lock`).

build pins: the git dependencies are built from source during `uv sync`, in an isolated build
environment whose backend uv resolves fresh from PyPI. That code runs at install time with network
access, so an unpinned backend is a supply-chain hole and makes the image non-reproducible, although
uv.lock pins every runtime package. [tool.uv] build-constraint-dependencies pins the backend and its
own dependencies (and uv-build, the projects' own backend, to the version CI uses). Tried: the
constraints are honored when the git dependency is built (uv -v shows setuptools>=84.0.0,<84.0.0+).
Prebuilding and hashing wheels was the alternative; it would take the git dependencies out of
uv.lock, which is worse. uv.lock records the constraints in its [manifest], so `uv sync --locked`
needs the lock refreshed after the patch: apply-pyproject-patches.sh does it.
Here: Orthonym (git) is built with hatchling and a build hook (hatch_build.py). The hook downloads the
two jars unless ORTHONYM_SKIP_JAR_PREFETCH=1, which services/chem already sets through
[tool.uv.extra-build-variables] and chem.Dockerfile exports as well.

--- a/services/chem/pyproject.toml
+++ b/services/chem/pyproject.toml
@@ -47,6 +47,20 @@
     "slow: runs the real Orthonym engine in a JVM (needs a Java 11+ runtime and the OPSIN and centres jars); select with -m slow",
 ]
 
+[tool.uv]
+# Build backends are pinned too (deploy/patches). Orthonym is built from source at
+# install time (hatchling with a build hook), in an isolated environment. Without this uv takes
+# the newest hatchling and its dependencies on PyPI that day and runs it. Versions: the newest releases
+# that were two weeks old on 2026-10-22. uv-build is the project's own backend (CI uses 0.13.5).
+build-constraint-dependencies = [
+    "hatchling==1.32.4",
+    "pathspec==1.1.1",
+    "pluggy==1.6.0",
+    "trove-classifiers==2026.9.21.13",
+    "packaging==26.3",
+    "uv-build==0.13.5",
+]
+
 [tool.uv.sources]
 decimer-service = { path = "../common", editable = true }
 orthonym = { git = "https://github.com/Steinbeck-Lab/Orthonym", rev = "110ed8153b365973ad90c518a3ea96fbebb13c8b" }
